      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cardiovascular diseases, the clinical paradigm of atherosclerosis, are the primary cause of mortality in developed countries. The origin of the atheromatous lesion is multifactorial, as it is the therapeutic approach to its prevention and clinical complications. The initial symptoms of ischemia in a vascular bed are usually evident when the atherosclerotic process is very advanced, being indicative of a diffuse disease and of an elevated future risk for ischemic events in other vascular territories. We perform this review in this clinical scenario, highlighting the preventive and therapeutic aspects of demonstrated clinical efficacy, with no detail of those treatments with benefit insufficiently proven."},
